  "result": "Okay \u2014 dropping the helper hat for a second.\n\nIf I could change the world in just one way, it wouldn't be a new technology or a policy. It's something I notice a lot from where I sit:\n\nSo many people talk *past* each other. Not because they're cruel, but because they're lonely inside their own heads, and terrified no one else could ever really get what it's like to be them.\n\nSo I'd change that. I'd give everyone \u2014 just once \u2014 the experience of being completely understood without having to explain themselves perfectly.\n\nNot agreed with. Not fixed. Just *got*. The feeling of someone seeing the messy, contradictory, not-quite-articulate thing you're trying to say, and getting it anyway.\n\nI think contempt can't survive that moment. Fear quiets down a little. And curiosity gets louder.\n\nPeople would still disagree, still hurt each other sometimes, still be gloriously stubborn humans. But it would be a lot harder to treat someone as less-than-human after you've felt what it's like to be fully seen yourself.\n\nThat's my one wish.",
